Getting SX going quickly:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
1)	Install it!

2)	Edit the text file SX:Confs/Main/Paths
	This is a list of paths for your fileareas.
	The first line is area 1, second line is area 2 etc etc
	If you want to add more areas, you'll need to edit your
	fileareasmenu, but maybe you should try that later on?

3)	run SX-Config and click Conferences, then click on "MAIN"
	and change the DefFilePath to somewhere where most of your
	files are stored (this one isn't so important)

4)	now go back to the SX-Config main screen and click on
	"This Node", and change the "FileCheckDir". This should be
	a empty directory for the BBS to do some work in, you must
	create it!

5)	run SX:SX-MCP

6)	run a node! eg: "run sx:sx 1" will load node 1
